   - p. The TPA has been set up only to divert or siphon off the funds within a group of companies or their associates. 

   - q. The TPA has failed to furnish additional information or clarifications called for by the Authority within  the time laid down, in connection with the application for renewal of TPA registration. 

- (2) Before taking action under regulation 16(1) of these regulations, the Authority shall grant a reasonable opportunity of being heard, to the TPA. 

- (3) However, the Authority may issue an order revoking or suspending the  Certificate of Registration without notice if the TPA; 

   - a. violates any one or more of the requirements under the Code of Conduct mentioned in Regulation 23 of these regulations; 

