Code of Conduct for TPAs; 

- 1) A TPA registered under these regulations shall act in the best professional manner. The Chief Executive Officer or the Chief Administrative Officer of a TPA shall be responsible for the proper day to day administration of a TPA as well as regulatory compliance issues. 

- 2) In particular and without prejudice to the generality of the provisions contained in these regulations, it shall be the duty of every TPA, its Chief Administrative Officer or Chief Executive Officer and Chief Medical Officer and its employees or representatives to 

   - a. establish their identity to the insured, claimant, policyholder and that of the insurer with which it has entered into an agreement, other entities and the public; . 

